---
import DocLayout from '../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<DocLayout title="Troubleshooting & FAQ">
  <h1>Troubleshooting & FAQ</h1>
  <p class="text-zinc-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-8 font-light">
    Find solutions to common performance questions, setup issues, and general lighting configuration queries.
  </p>

  <div class="space-y-8">
    <!-- Section: Core FAQs -->
    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-white text-base font-semibold mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
        <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-technical-amber" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M8.228 9c.549-1.165 2.03-2 3.772-2 2.21 0 4 1.343 4 3 0 1.4-1.278 2.575-3.006 2.907-.542.104-.994.54-.994 1.093m0 3h.01M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" />
        </svg>
        Frequently Asked Questions
      </h2>

      <div class="space-y-4">
        <!-- Q1 -->
        <div class="bg-white/[0.01] border border-white/5 p-6 rounded-2xl hover:border-amber-500/20 hover:bg-white/[0.02] transition-all duration-300">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-medium text-white mb-2 flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-technical-amber font-mono select-none">Q:</span>
            <span>Why is "No Shader Preview Rendered" showing in the list?</span>
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed font-light pl-6">
            Generate the preview by clicking the <strong>File Refresh</strong> button
            <span class="inline-flex items-center justify-center p-1 bg-white/5 border border-white/10 rounded ml-1 mr-1 align-middle">
              <img
                src={`${base}icons/blender/file_refresh.svg`}
                alt="File Refresh"
                class="w-3.5 h-3.5"
              />
            </span>
            next to the material path in the manager interface. Previews are not compiled automatically for standard parameter inputs.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Q2 -->
        <div class="bg-white/[0.01] border border-white/5 p-6 rounded-2xl hover:border-amber-500/20 hover:bg-white/[0.02] transition-all duration-300">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-medium text-white mb-2 flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-technical-amber font-mono select-none">Q:</span>
            <span>Why is my Mesh Light / Emissive object missing from the list?</span>
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed font-light pl-6">
            Verify if the object has been marked as an emissive object within the addon interface. By default, for performance reasons, the addon does not automatically scan all scene materials in real-time, so this marking must be done manually in some cases. Also, ensure the mesh name or material name matches your configured filter keywords (such as <code>glow</code> or <code>emit</code>) in the Addon Preferences.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Q3 -->
        <div class="bg-white/[0.01] border border-white/5 p-6 rounded-2xl hover:border-amber-500/20 hover:bg-white/[0.02] transition-all duration-300">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-medium text-white mb-2 flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-technical-amber font-mono select-none">Q:</span>
            <span>How are Custom Presets persistent across Blender updates?</span>
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed font-light pl-6">
            Custom presets are saved outside of the addon directory in Blender's persistent configuration path (<code>.../config/scene_light_manager/presets/</code>). This ensures your rigs are safe and preserved even when updating or reinstalling the addon.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Q4 -->
        <div class="bg-white/[0.01] border border-white/5 p-6 rounded-2xl hover:border-amber-500/20 hover:bg-white/[0.02] transition-all duration-300">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-medium text-white mb-2 flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-technical-amber font-mono select-none">Q:</span>
            <span>Why are the SLM gizmos/Smart Buttons not showing up?</span>
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed font-light pl-6">
            Ensure that Blender's global <strong>Show Gizmos</strong> toggle (icon in the top-right header of the 3D Viewport) is turned on. Also, verify that a supported Light object (Area, Spot, Point, or Sun) is actively selected.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section: Performance & Setup Troubleshooting -->
    <section class="space-y-4 pt-4">
      <h2 class="text-white text-base font-semibold mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
        <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-technical-amber" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 9v2m0 4h.01m-6.938 4h13.856c1.54 0 2.502-1.667 1.732-3L13.732 4c-.77-1.333-2.694-1.333-3.464 0L3.34 16c-.77 1.333.192 3 1.732 3z" />
        </svg>
        Performance & Setup Troubleshooting
      </h2>

      <div class="space-y-4">
        <!-- T1 -->
        <div class="bg-white/[0.01] border border-white/5 p-6 rounded-2xl hover:border-amber-500/20 hover:bg-white/[0.02] transition-all duration-300 flex gap-4">
          <div class="p-2 rounded-lg bg-amber-500/5 text-amber-400 border border-amber-500/10 h-fit">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-2">
            <h3 class="text-sm font-medium text-white">Viewport Lag during Slider Tweak</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed font-light">
              If adjusting exposure or colors causes micro-stuttering, ensure <strong>Cycles GPU</strong> is set as the active Preview Render Engine in Addon Preferences. Cycles performs asynchronous background renders, whereas EEVEE compiles shaders synchronously on Blender's main thread, causing frames to drop.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- T2 -->
        <div class="bg-white/[0.01] border border-white/5 p-6 rounded-2xl hover:border-amber-500/20 hover:bg-white/[0.02] transition-all duration-300 flex gap-4">
          <div class="p-2 rounded-lg bg-amber-500/5 text-amber-400 border border-amber-500/10 h-fit">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M18.364 18.364A9 9 0 005.636 5.636m12.728 12.728A9 9 0 015.636 5.636m12.728 12.728L5.636 5.636" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-2">
            <h3 class="text-sm font-medium text-white">Shading Artifacts on Texture Maps</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed font-light">
              Ensure your working color space is configured correctly. Working in color spaces other than linear (such as sRGB on non-color maps) can distort normal outputs and shadow orientations. If necessary, use the diagnostics panel to reset mapping coordinates.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- T3 -->
        <div class="bg-white/[0.01] border border-white/5 p-6 rounded-2xl hover:border-amber-500/20 hover:bg-white/[0.02] transition-all duration-300 flex gap-4">
          <div class="p-2 rounded-lg bg-amber-500/5 text-amber-400 border border-amber-500/10 h-fit">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15 12a3 3 0 1 1-6 0 3 3 0 0 1 6 0Z" />
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M2.458 12C3.732 7.943 7.523 5 12 5c4.478 0 8.268 2.943 9.542 7-1.274 4.057-5.064 7-9.542 7-4.477 0-8.268-2.943-9.542-7z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-2">
            <h3 class="text-sm font-medium text-white">Light and Shadow Linking does not show viewport outlines</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed font-light">
              To display the highlight/outline effect on linked objects in the 3D viewport, make sure the checkbox option <strong>Highlight Linked/Blockers in viewport</strong> is turned on in the addon interface. Modern Blender versions support light and shadow linking under both EEVEE and Cycles rendering engines.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- T4 -->
        <div class="bg-white/[0.01] border border-white/5 p-6 rounded-2xl hover:border-amber-500/20 hover:bg-white/[0.02] transition-all duration-300 flex gap-4">
          <div class="p-2 rounded-lg bg-amber-500/5 text-amber-400 border border-amber-500/10 h-fit">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M11 5H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v11a2 2 0 002 2h11a2 2 0 002-2v-5m-1.414-9.414a2 2 0 112.828 2.828L11.828 15H9v-2.828l8.586-8.586z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-2">
            <h3 class="text-sm font-medium text-white">The HDRI Rotation Shortcut conflicts with viewport navigation</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed font-light">
              If the default <code>Ctrl + Alt + RMB</code> shortcut clashes with other custom plugins or your native OS navigation, you can rebind it under <strong>Edit > Preferences > Keymap</strong> (search for <code>Scene Light Manager</code>), or adjust the environment angle using the slider in the unified sidebar's World tab.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section: Support callout -->
    <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-amber-500/5 to-orange-500/5 border border-amber-500/10 rounded-2xl p-8 text-center relative overflow-hidden mt-8">
      <div class="absolute -right-16 -bottom-16 w-48 h-48 rounded-full bg-amber-500/5 blur-2xl pointer-events-none"></div>
      <h3 class="text-white text-base font-semibold mb-2">Still Need Help?</h3>
      <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 max-w-md mx-auto mb-6 font-light">
        If you couldn't find an answer here, feel free to report bug issues directly on GitHub or contact support via email.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-4">
        <a 
          href="mailto:kezives3d@gmail.com" 
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-5 py-2.5 rounded-full bg-white text-zinc-950 font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest font-semibold hover:bg-zinc-200 transition-all duration-300 shadow-lg shadow-white/5"
          style="color: #09090b !important; text-decoration: none !important;"
        >
          <span>Email Support</span>
        </a>
        <a 
          href="https://github.com/r-kez/k_tools_slm_documentation/issues" 
          target="_blank" 
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-5 py-2.5 rounded-full bg-zinc-900 border border-white/10 text-white font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest font-semibold hover:bg-zinc-800 transition-all duration-300"
          style="text-decoration: none !important;"
        >
          <span>Open GitHub Issue</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</DocLayout>
